; --anon builds its copy of a transaction one posting at a time, upstream
; of the rewrite rules.  Every posting of a rewritten transaction must join
; the one copy the rules made for it, so register shows the payee once and
; print shows each transaction once with all its postings.  The rules match
; every hashed name, so the output does not depend on the hashes.  The
; expected output is the output of the same command, without --anon and
; the rules, on this journal with payee Shop, every account X and the
; commodity $ written A.

2024/01/01 Grocer
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Landlord
    Expenses:Rent    $500.00
    Expenses:Fees      $5.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg --anon --payee-rewrite .=Shop --account-rewrite .=X
24-Jan-01 Shop                  X                            A10.00       A10.00
                                X                           A-10.00            0
24-Jan-02 Shop                  X                           A500.00      A500.00
                                X                             A5.00      A505.00
                                X                          A-505.00            0
end test

test print --anon --payee-rewrite .=Shop --account-rewrite .=X
2024/01/01 Shop
    X                                         A10.00
    X

2024/01/02 Shop
    X                                        A500.00
    X                                          A5.00
    X
end test
